WHY A WIDENING (not a new concept, not a Story rewrite)
The step "halve twice" is already a right-kind `when` action on the existing
Public interface item Halve, and a `when` concept for that item and that kind of
use already exists ("halve"). It failed only because that concept's prose is
closed at a single halving ("Halve the entered number once."), so a second press
falls outside its stated meaning. The product description already states the
supported range — "exactly one or two Halve presses per request: one displays
half the entered number; two displays its quarter. Three or more presses are not
supported." — so the concept prose is narrower than the product it describes.
The repair is therefore to add the second-press variation to the existing
concept's closed prose. The Story needs no rewrite: "halve twice" is the correct
wording for the intended behaviour.

